From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 23:34:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 187/209] feat(entity): authored area fade distance

An area's near band - the ENTERNEARAREA / MOVENEARAREA band, and with it the
area's footprint in CAreaGrid - was never a property of the area. CArea's
three fade getters (GetFadeDistance, GetEnvironmentFadeDistance,
GetGreatestFadeDistance) each compute the maximum over the entities LINKED to
the area, reading IEntityAudioComponent::Get*FadeDistance() off every one of
them. An area could therefore only have a near band if something audio-shaped
was linked to it, which is the coupling that forces every consumer that wants
a fade to pretend to be audio.

Add an authored value beside it:

- IEntityAreaComponent::SetFadeDistance / GetFadeDistance, two new virtuals
  appended at the end of the interface (append-only, it crosses DLLs).
- CArea::m_authoredFadeDistance, 0 by default, set through
  CArea::SetAuthoredFadeDistance().
- The three getters seed their maximum with it instead of with 0, i.e. they
  now return max(authored, max-over-linked).

Legacy arithmetic is unchanged: the default is 0 and max(0, x) == x, so every
existing area computes exactly the value it computed before, and nothing in
the tree calls the new setter yet.

The setter invalidates the three cached maxima (negative means "not computed
yet" outside the editor) and calls SetAreaDirty(), so a fade authored after
the grid was built re-registers the area with its new footprint - otherwise
CAreaGrid::AddArea, which sizes the footprint from GetGreatestFadeDistance(),
would keep the old one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
